// A namespace import (`use @Std/Core`, no `only`) loads the module but binds no
// flat names. Calling `assert` as a bare name relies on the old flat namespace and
// must be rejected (spec/15: a cross-module function is visible only when imported
// with `only { … }`). The fix is `use @Std/Core only { assert }`.
use @Std/Core

fn main() {
    assert(true)
}
